  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 1, 'Pause for one slow breath before you answer the next email after you notice a mistake in the last one.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 2, 'Tell the person your slip affects within the hour, in one plain sentence about what happened.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 3, 'Write three short lines about a recent slip: what happened, what helped, and what you would try next time.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 4, 'When you catch yourself replaying the typo in this morning''s email, call it a rerun and switch on a podcast instead.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 5, 'Burn the toast? Scrape off the dark bits over the sink, shrug, and enjoy your breakfast anyway.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 6, 'Take three slow breaths at your desk the moment you spot a typo you already sent.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 7, 'Resend the email with the right attachment and a short note saying the first one was missing it.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 8, 'Start a page titled "Lessons" in a notebook or notes app, and add one thing a recent mistake taught you.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 9, 'Give the awkward thing you said at lunch ten minutes on a kitchen timer, then close the notebook when it rings.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 10, 'Take a wrong turn on your walk and explore the new street for a few minutes before heading back.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 11, 'Name the slip in one plain sentence, such as "I forgot the milk," with no insults added.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 12, 'Replace the mug you chipped at a friend''s place with one you think they would enjoy.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 13, 'Pick one task you often rush and add a single checkbox to it, such as rereading the address before you hit send.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 14, 'Ask yourself whether the late bill you paid today will matter a year from now, and write your honest answer on a sticky note.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 15, 'Leave a harmless typo in a sent text alone instead of sending three corrections after it.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 16, 'Notice where the hot-faced feeling sits in your body after a mistake, and simply point to it.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 17, 'Post the correct fact in the group chat where you shared a wrong one, along with where you checked it.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 18, 'Ask a coworker you trust for one piece of honest feedback on something you handed in recently.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 19, 'Picture a friend who forgot a coworker''s name in a meeting, and say aloud the kind words you would offer them about your own slip.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 20, 'Ask for a name you forgot with a simple "Remind me your name?" and then use it warmly once.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 21, 'Place a hand on your chest after a small kitchen spill and feel it rise and fall three times.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 22, 'Offer one concrete fix as you own the slip, such as redoing the slides by noon.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 23, 'Notice whether your last slip happened when you were hungry, tired or rushed, and jot down which one.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 24, 'Write the wrong order you placed for the team on a scrap of paper, then tear it into small pieces and toss them in the recycling.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 25, 'Grab a towel after a spilled drink, say "Oops," and skip the long apology.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 26, 'Say "okay, that happened" out loud, quietly, the next time you drop something at home.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 27, 'Ask "Is there anything else I can do?" after you fix something, and listen to the whole answer.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 28, 'Read back an old mistake from years ago and name one good habit it left you with.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 29, 'Knead bread dough or a ball of clay for fifteen minutes after a clumsy moment at work, letting your hands take over from your thoughts.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 30, 'Missed the bus? Use the wait to look around the stop and notice three things you usually rush past.'),
  ('bouncing-back-from-mistakes', 31, 'Step outside for one minute after a tense mistake at work and look up at the sky.'),
